{"name":"Haddock’s Sweater","hex":"#277aba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"haddock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A saltwater fish, Melanogrammus aeglefinus, of the North Atlantic, important as a food fish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haddock"},{"term":"sweater","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A knitted jacket or jersey, usually of thick wool, worn by athletes before or after exercise.","A similar garment worn for warmth."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dress in a sweater."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweater"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweater","blocks":[{"text":"A sweater or pullover, also called a jersey or jumper, is a piece of clothing, typically with long sleeves, made of knitted or crocheted material that covers the upper part of the body. When sleeveless, the garment is often called a slipover, tank top, or sweater vest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Selburose-sweater.jpg/330px-Selburose-sweater.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweater","wikidata":"Q232191"},{"title":"Haddock","blocks":[{"text":"The haddock is a saltwater ray-finned fish from the family Gadidae, the true cods. It is the only species in the monotypic genus Melanogrammus. It is found in the North Atlantic Ocean and associated seas, where it is an important species for fisheries, especially in northern Europe, where it is marketed fresh, frozen and smoked; smoked varieties include the Finnan haddie and the Arbroath smokie. Other smoked versions include long boneless, the filleted side of larger haddock smoked in oak chips with the skin left on the fillet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Haddock%2C_Boston_Aquarium.JPG/330px-Haddock%2C_Boston_Aquarium.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikip